  "findings": [
    "Default omitted/null jb.safe_delete file selection now routes to the explicit captured_es_module_functions_v1 policy for writable .ts TypeScript or .js JavaScript ES modules containing named functions and at least one export. Other declaration shapes/languages and propagation refuse. Explicit forced-file deletion retains its visible skipped-usage behavior, and file/symbol selectors, edit permissions, host grants and standard guarded plan/application/recovery remain distinct.",
    "Native syntax/byte/entity admission, conservative graph/path/name candidates and full captured text hashes precede selected provider definition/reference checks. Every declaration requires one exact self-bound definition and a bounded reference response including that declaration; all references must be inside the selected file. Missing/empty/truncated/foreign replies or inconsistent provider/source context refuse without publishing a plan. Provider source omissions and host passive/execution policy remain visible. No default model, provider command or analyzed-project execution is introduced.",
    "Limits admit at most2000 files,16000000 captured bytes counted per physical file,256000 selected module bytes and8 declarations, producing at most16 provider queries. The initial 2000-file case failed under the unchanged30s deadline because each literal read rebuilt the captured source scope. A separate actual diagnostic RED records Request deadline exceeded after31.03s of test runtime. Only the private loop changes to one admitted CapturedSourceScope with source_in_scope; every path, membership, size, hash and cancellation check remains. Identical2000/2001 assertions and deadline then pass, alongside16m/16m+1 and8/9 boundaries. This is an owned boundary observation, not a universal performance claim.",
    "Final scoped regression records63 passed/1 failed/0 ignored across6 groups; all9 new cases pass. The remaining failure is the unchanged actual OS1314 forced-delete symlink setup before assertions. The separate actual installed TypeScript language-server/compiler gate contains two owned TypeScript/JavaScript fixtures; both repair-free unused-module plans, copied-result compilation, approved application, exact recovery and used-module refusals pass. It is one Rust test and remains nonadditive.",
    "Initial library425/0/7 and other initial regressions use the earlier private bulk-loop source; they are retained as separate observations. Only the new private loop and test diagnostic differ between those scoped source maps. Final all-target Clippy passes, and550 scoped runtime inputs match the integrated checkout by exact bytes or explicitly recorded CRLF materialization. Integrated formatting, Python17, mandatory typecheck and TypeScript260/3 existing skips pass with all final integration inputs unchanged. No whole-native rerun or hosted/platform acceptance follows.",
    "The result keeps complete=false, exhaustiveCompilerProof=false and remainingUsagesMayBreak=true. Captured path/name matches conservatively deny possible usage and can reject unrelated prose; dynamic, omitted, external and differently configured consumers remain unknown. Host-selected provider replies are observations, not execution attestation or exhaustive absence proof. All353 original inventory identities,73 unreconciled rows,77 backend unknowns and false full-contract certifications remain. Broader R1-R9, full upstream/parity, packaging, main merge and release stay open."
  ],
